From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: deactivate the window when a host focus loss can't set the desktop foreground.

When the host takes the keyboard focus to a non-Wine window, winewayland
makes the desktop window the foreground window. In an AION 2 run (#877),
that set_foreground_window() call failed, so the game stayed the
foreground and active window in the background and never muted. Fall
back to deactivating the window in that case, so the application still
gets its deactivation messages; returning to it makes it foreground
again through the host keyboard enter.

Also log the target window's thread and the error code of failed
foreground changes on the focus channel, to find out why it fails.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/input.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/input.c
@@ -2363,7 +2363,8 @@
 
     TRACE( "hwnd %p, mouse %u, internal %u -> ret %u, previous %p\n", hwnd, mouse, internal, ret, previous );
     if (!ret || previous != hwnd)
-        TRACE_(focus)( "foreground %p -> %p, mouse %u, internal %u, ret %u\n", previous, hwnd, mouse, internal, ret );
+        TRACE_(focus)( "foreground %p -> %p (thread %04x), mouse %u, internal %u, ret %u, error %u\n", previous, hwnd,
+                       (int)new_thread_id, mouse, internal, ret, ret ? 0 : (int)RtlGetLastWin32Error() );
 
     if (ret && previous != hwnd)
     {
--- a/dlls/win32u/message.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/message.c
@@ -2305,7 +2305,15 @@
         if (foreground)
         {
             TRACE_(focus)( "host state change on %p sets foreground %p\n", hwnd, foreground );
-            set_foreground_window( foreground, FALSE, TRUE );
+            /* The host focus moved to a non-Wine window, but the desktop window
+             * couldn't be made foreground. Still deactivate the window that lost
+             * it, so that the application knows it is in the background. */
+            if (!set_foreground_window( foreground, FALSE, TRUE ) && foreground == get_desktop_window() &&
+                hwnd == NtUserGetForegroundWindow())
+            {
+                TRACE_(focus)( "deactivating %p instead\n", hwnd );
+                NtUserSetActiveWindow( 0 );
+            }
         }
         switch (LOWORD(state_cmd))
         {
